<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort de la Roche</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1640</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort de la <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoffmann-la-roche">Roche</a> was a stronghold built around 1640 by the Huguenot engineer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-le-vasseur">Jean Le Vasseur</a> on a rock above the harbour of Tortuga, off northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>. Reached by an iron ladder and armed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a>, it let the French hold the island against Spanish attack, repelling an assault in 1643, and made Tortuga a secure base for buccaneers. Spanish forces captured it in 1654.</p></div>
